<section class="sec" id="s-about"><div class="wrap"><p class="eye rv">01 · the studio</p><h2 class="st pop">We run the operations and write the software.</h2><p class="sl rv" style="--i:2">So every system is built from the floor up, for the people who actually use it: dispatch staff in a cold room, kitchen teams on a rush, outlet managers, a finance team at month-end.</p>
 <div class="facts" data-stag=""><div class="fc" style="--c:var(--cy);--glow:rgba(14,124,134,.16)"><i class="ti ti-arrows-exchange" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="k">Operations + software</span><h3 class="pop">Both sides of the problem</h3><p>We sit inside the operation and write the code, so the tool fits how the work is actually done, not how a spec imagines it.</p></div><div class="fc" style="--c:var(--pk);--glow:rgba(194,54,107,.14)"><i class="ti ti-building-factory-2" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="k">In production</span><h3 class="pop">Six systems, daily use</h3><p>Across food manufacturing and retail: inspection, dispatch, monitoring, finance and logistics. Each one replaced a manual job.</p></div><div class="fc" style="--c:var(--lm);--glow:rgba(79,143,31,.14)"><i class="ti ti-snowflake" aria-hidden="true"></i><span class="k">Built on the floor</span><h3 class="pop">Works in gloves, offline</h3><p>Rugged scanners at −4 °C, edge devices that run without a network, agents that start themselves. Reliability over polish.</p></div></div>
