var C={inspector:{k:'Case 01 / 06 — computer vision and edge AI',lead:'A Linux inspection machine photographs food, grades its quality with AI, and returns a pass, downgrade or reject verdict in seconds. A dashboard shows the trend, and a kitchen display checks every delivery plate against its reference photo before it leaves.',role:'Design, hardware setup, AI model, web apps',stack:'Linux · Python · OpenCV · PyTorch/ONNX · Node.js · Supabase · Vercel',prob:['Food quality was judged by eye. Two inspectors could grade the same batch differently, results changed from shift to shift, and nothing was recorded. If a customer complained, there was no photo or score to look back at.','In the kitchen, plates for delivery orders were checked by whoever was free, so missing items and poor presentation reached customers. The goal was one consistent, recorded judgement for every item and every plate.'],cons:['24×7 industrial use','No GPU on the floor','Must grade when the network drops','Nothing to install for staff'],bef:[['Inspect by eye','Two inspectors could grade the same batch differently.'],['No record','Results changed shift to shift; nothing written down.'],['Complaints without evidence','No photo or score to look back at.'],['Plates checked ad hoc','Whoever was free checked plates, so misses reached customers.']],flow:[['Capture','Fixed lighting and camera position, so every sample is photographed the same way.'],['Pre-process','Crop, white-balance and normalise the frame on the device.'],['Detect','The model finds the item and reads colour, texture, blemishes and shape.'],['Score','Features roll up into a 0–100 score, weighted per food type.',1],['Verdict','Pass, downgrade or reject, saved with the image for audit and re-training.']],note:'Verdict scale: pass (grade A) · downgrade (grade B) · reject.',parts:[['Edge device','Inspection machine','Linux edge device with an industrial camera in a light-controlled chamber. The model runs on the device, so grading works even if the network drops.'],['Web app','Management dashboard','Every inspection with photo, score and verdict. Live counts and trends by food type, batch and shift, down to a single item.'],['Web app','Kitchen display','Live Zomato and Swiggy orders. The camera capture appears beside the reference image and the AI flags missing or off-standard items before the order leaves.']],dec:[['Run the model on the device (ONNX)','Grading keeps working offline, in real time on modest hardware, with no GPU on the floor.','The model has to fit the device; training stays flexible in PyTorch, inference is constrained by hardware.'],['Control the input before improving the model','Fixed chamber, lighting and camera: the same item photographs the same way any day.','A physical rig to build and maintain, for far more stable scores.'],['One Supabase backend for machine, dashboard and KDS','Postgres, auth and storage in one place; the photo stored next to its verdict.','A single shared dependency, in return for one source of truth.'],['Web apps on Vercel','Open on any laptop or tablet with nothing to install; updates live in minutes.','The apps need a connection; the grading does not.']],ops:[[1,'Grading survives network loss','The model runs on the device, so verdicts continue when the connection is down.'],[1,'Services restart themselves','Linux runs headless for 24×7 use; services come back without a person.'],[1,'Every verdict is auditable','The photo is saved with score and verdict, for disputes and re-training.'],[0,'Watch for input drift','Lighting or camera drift shifts scores more than any model change; rig consistency is treated as an operational check.']],res:[['Same judgement, every shift','Every item is scored against identical criteria, and every score is recorded with its photo.'],['Caught before dispatch','The plating check flags problems while the plate is still in the kitchen, not after a complaint.'],['Quality is visible','Managers see trends per line, batch and shift from anywhere, and the logged data keeps improving the model.']],tools:[['Linux','Runs the camera, model and services on the machine.','Stable for 24×7 industrial use, runs headless, services restart themselves.'],['Python and OpenCV','Captures frames, corrects light and colour, crops the item for the model.','Makes every sample look the same to the model: the biggest factor in consistent scores.'],['PyTorch and ONNX','Trains the quality model; ONNX runs it fast on the device.','Flexible training, real-time inference on modest hardware, no GPU needed.'],['Industrial camera and rig','Produces consistent images in the chamber.','Consistent input beats a smarter model; the same tomato gets the same score any day.'],['Supabase','Stores every inspection, image, order and comparison; handles login.','Postgres, auth and storage in one place, shared by the machine, dashboard and KDS.'],['Node.js web stack','The dashboard, the KDS and the API layer.','Opens on any laptop or tablet in the plant or kitchen with nothing to install.'],['Vercel','Hosts the dashboard and KDS.','Push-to-deploy; updates go live in minutes with no server to maintain.']]},
dispatch:{k:'Case 02 / 06 — Android and ERP automation',lead:'Stock leaves the cold rooms every day for outlets and vendors. The team scans the order on a Honeywell handheld and presses submit; the whole order posts into PACT ERP under one voucher number, and that voucher comes back to the scanner.',role:'Android app, cloud backend, PACT automation',stack:'Android (Java) · Honeywell · Supabase · AWS EC2 · S3 · Vercel · PACT ERP',prob:['Every dispatch was written on paper at the cold room and typed into PACT later by hand. That meant duplicate work, typing mistakes, stock figures that were only trustworthy after an end-of-day reconciliation, and no way to know which outlet had received what until the next morning.','The system had to remove the typing entirely while staying simple enough for floor staff working in gloves at −4 °C.'],cons:['Gloves at −4 °C','PACT has no public API','Cold-room network can drop','Billing must stay in PACT'],bef:[['Written on paper','Each dispatch noted by hand at the cold room.'],['Typed into PACT later','Duplicate work and typing mistakes.'],['Trusted at end of day','Stock figures only reliable after reconciliation.'],['Blind until morning','No way to know which outlet received what.']],flow:[['Scan and submit','The app lists pending orders; the team scans each item. On submit it saves a local copy and drops the order into the cloud inbox.',0,'1–2 s'],['Cloud inbox','A secure Supabase queue holds each order. A watcher polls it every few seconds.',0,'~6 s to pick-up'],['PACT worker posts','An always-on EC2 machine opens the stock-outward screen, enters every item and posts a single voucher.',1,'1–3 min'],['Voucher back','The voucher number returns to the scanner and the order is locked against re-scanning.',0,'total 1½–4 min']],parts:[['Sync','Auto-refresh','Every 15 minutes in business hours the system pulls new orders and updated quantities from PACT. No manual sync.'],['Logic','Pending maths','Ordered minus already dispatched, so the team only sees what still needs scanning.'],['Watcher','Inbox watcher','The PACT worker never sleeps; an order submitted at any hour is caught within seconds.'],['Guards','Safety checks','One voucher per order, duplicate submits ignored, order numbers validated, completed orders locked.']],dec:[['Drive PACT\u2019s screen from a dedicated worker','PACT has no public API, so an always-on EC2 machine operates the stock-outward screen like a person would.','Posting takes 1–3 minutes rather than milliseconds, and the worker depends on that screen staying as it is.'],['Put a cloud inbox between the scanner and the ERP','The handheld never waits on PACT: it saves a local copy, drops the order in the queue and moves on.','Posting is near-real-time, not instant; the voucher arrives a few minutes later.'],['Integrate PACT, don\u2019t replace it','Billing stays in the system finance trusts; only the typing is removed.','The system inherits PACT\u2019s pace and screens instead of designing its own.'],['Honeywell handhelds with a native Android (Java) app','Cold-resistant, glove-friendly, direct access to the imager; offline queuing if the network drops.','A native app to maintain, in exchange for fast scans at −4 °C.']],ops:[[1,'Local copy + offline queue','Submit saves a local copy; the app queues offline if the cold-room network drops.'],[1,'Duplicate submits ignored','One voucher per order; completed orders are locked against re-scanning.'],[1,'Order numbers validated','Only validated orders reach PACT.'],[0,'Bounded retry on worker faults','Shown in the simulator as a design consideration; not a documented feature of the deployed worker.']],sim:1,res:[['Submit to voucher in 1½–4 min','The full journey finishes while the team loads the next crate, with a voucher on the scanner as proof.'],['Zero manual PACT entry','Nobody on the floor opens PACT. Stock is adjusted at the moment of scanning, not at end of day.'],['No wrong bills','One voucher per order, no double posting, only validated orders reach PACT.']],tools:[['Android (Java)','The scanning app: order list, scanning, submit, voucher.','Direct access to the Honeywell imager and offline queuing if the cold-room network drops.'],['Honeywell scanners','The only device the team touches.','Cold-resistant, glove-friendly, built-in imager. Fast scans at −4 °C are the foundation.'],['Supabase','The cloud inbox and the record of every order, scan and voucher.','One source of truth for the app, the worker and the dashboard, with no custom storage API.'],['Amazon S3','Keeps dispatch files, proofs and exports.','Cheap, durable storage that never fills a server disk, linked from every order.'],['AWS EC2','The always-on worker that drives PACT\u2019s stock-outward screen.','PACT has no public API, so a dedicated machine operating it like a person is the reliable way to post.'],['Vercel','Hosts the dashboard and keeps the order list current.','Zero-maintenance hosting; supervisors open a URL and see what left, when and for whom.'],['PACT ERP','Where the final voucher and stock live.','Integrated, not replaced. Billing stays in the system finance trusts.']]},
music:{k:'Case 03 / 06 — Python agents and monitoring',lead:'A Python agent on every outlet laptop and a master console we run. It reports whether each outlet is playing licensed music through our UCA subscription, at the right volume, and for how long each day, without asking staff to do anything.',role:'Agent, master console, reporting',stack:'Python · Windows startup service · Supabase · Vercel',prob:['We pay for a UCA-based subscription so outlets can legally play curated music. In practice, staff often didn\u2019t start it, played random YouTube instead (a licensing risk and off-brand), left the volume wrong, or ran the outlet in silence.','Visiting each outlet was impossible and self-reporting didn\u2019t work. We needed to see, from one screen, what was actually happening everywhere.'],cons:['Nothing for staff to do','Many outlets, one screen','Must survive laptop restarts'],bef:[['Subscription paid','Licensed, curated music available at every outlet.'],['Often not started','Random YouTube instead, a licensing risk and off-brand.'],['Wrong volume or silence','No consistent atmosphere across outlets.'],['No way to know','Visits impossible, self-reporting unreliable.']],flow:[['Starts with the laptop','The agent launches at boot as a background process. Staff never see it or open it.'],['Checks every few minutes','Is the laptop on? Is audio playing? From the UCA app or another source? Is the volume in band?',1],['Reports to the cloud','Each check is written to Supabase with outlet ID and timestamp. Missed reports mean the laptop is off.'],['Master console','One screen shows every outlet live, flags problems, and totals playback minutes per day.']],note:'Recorded per outlet: source app, playing or silent, volume level, minutes played today, and time since last check-in.',dec:[['Start at boot, stay invisible','A Windows startup service launches the agent whenever the laptop turns on. If the laptop is on, monitoring is on.','The agent has to be installed once on every outlet laptop.'],['Design the heartbeat so silence is a signal','Every check-in carries an outlet ID and timestamp; a gap in check-ins means the laptop is off.','"Off" and "agent broken" look the same from the console until someone checks the outlet.'],['Python for the Windows audio stack','Reads the audio session, process list and volume mixer with small libraries; one script runs everywhere.','Tied to Windows; a different OS would need its own agent.']],ops:[[1,'Missed check-ins are visible','Time since last check-in is recorded per outlet; a gap is itself the alert.'],[1,'Non-UCA sources flagged','Unlicensed playback is caught the same day.'],[1,'Volume and silence tracked','Out-of-band volume and silent periods show on the console.'],[1,'Managers self-serve','Each manager checks their own outlet from a phone, nothing to install.']],res:[['Full visibility, zero visits','One screen shows what every outlet is playing now and how long it played today.'],['Licensing risk closed','Non-UCA sources are flagged immediately, so unlicensed playback is caught the same day.'],['Consistent atmosphere','Volume out of band and silent periods are visible, so every outlet sounds the way the brand intends.']],tools:[['Python','The outlet agent and the master console.','Reads the Windows audio session, process list and volume mixer with small libraries; one script runs everywhere.'],['Windows startup service','Launches the agent when the laptop turns on.','Removes the human step. If the laptop is on, monitoring is on.'],['Supabase','Receives every check-in and stores the history.','One table all agents write to; a gap in check-ins is itself a signal.'],['Vercel','Hosts a web view for outlet managers.','Managers check their own outlet from a phone, with nothing to install.']]},
ledger:{k:'Case 04 / 06 — finance automation',lead:'A desktop tool that reconciles a ledger against its bills automatically: matching entries, flagging what doesn\u2019t tie out, and exporting a balanced statement. The finance team spends minutes on exceptions instead of hours on line-by-line checks.',role:'Design and build',stack:'Python · Excel and CSV pipelines · Supabase',prob:['Balancing a ledger meant placing the export next to a stack of bills and ticking off entries one by one. It was slow, mistakes hid among hundreds of rows, and month-end always ran late.','The team didn\u2019t need a new accounting system. They needed the tedious matching done for them so they could focus on the handful of entries that actually disagreed.'],cons:['Finance lives in Excel','No new accounting system','Hundreds of rows per ledger'],bef:[['Export beside the bills','Ledger printout next to a stack of paper bills.'],['Tick off one by one','Every entry checked by hand.'],['Mistakes hide','Among hundreds of rows, errors go unnoticed.'],['Month-end runs late','Every time.']],flow:[['Import','Load the ledger export and the bill list (Excel or CSV) for a vendor, outlet or period.'],['Auto-match','Entries are matched on bill number, date and amount, with tolerance rules for rounding and partial payments.',1],['Exceptions','Everything that doesn\u2019t tie out is listed by type: missing bill, duplicate, amount difference, wrong date.'],['Balance and export','The team resolves exceptions and exports a balanced statement with a clear audit trail.']],note:'Exception types reported: bill missing from ledger, ledger entry without a bill, amount differs beyond tolerance, duplicate entry, date mismatch.',dec:[['Match with tolerance rules, not exact equality','Rounding and partial payments are matched by rule instead of becoming false exceptions.','Tolerances have to be set carefully so a real difference isn\u2019t absorbed as rounding.'],['Meet finance in Excel and CSV','Input and output in the formats the team already works in meant no training and immediate adoption.','File-based rather than a live connection to the accounting system.'],['Keep a history of every run in Supabase','Past runs can be reopened, and recurring problem vendors become visible over time.','A desktop tool that also needs a cloud record; worth it for the audit trail.']],ops:[[1,'Exceptions are typed','Missing bill, entry without bill, amount beyond tolerance, duplicate, date mismatch: each named so it can be worked quickly.'],[1,'Resolution is recorded','Each run leaves a record of what matched, what didn\u2019t, and how it was resolved.'],[1,'Problem vendors surface','Run history makes recurring mismatches visible over time.']],res:[['Matching in minutes','The bulk of entries tie out automatically; the team only works the exception list.'],['Fewer missed errors','Duplicates and amount differences are surfaced by the tool, not left to someone spotting them.'],['Cleaner month-end','Each run leaves a clear record of what matched, what didn\u2019t, and how it was resolved.']],tools:[['Python','Reads the files, runs the matching, builds the exceptions and the export.','Thousands of rows with matching rules is what Python\u2019s data libraries are built for, and the rules are easy to adjust.'],['Excel and CSV','Input and output formats.','Finance already works in Excel, so meeting them there meant no training and immediate adoption.'],['Supabase','Keeps a history of every reconciliation run.','Past runs can be reopened, and recurring problem vendors become visible over time.']]},
bills:{k:'Case 05 / 06 — document extraction and ERP automation',lead:'Upload a vendor bill and the goods-received entry is created in PACT on its own. Items and quantities are read from the bill, matched to the sales order, and inventory adjusts with no manual typing. The inbound twin of the dispatch system.',role:'Web app, bill reading, PACT automation',stack:'Node.js · Python · AWS EC2 · S3 · Supabase · Vercel · PACT ERP',prob:['After dispatch removed the typing on the way out, the way in was still manual: every vendor bill was read by a person and keyed into PACT as a stock-inward entry. Goods sat before stock figures caught up, and typing errors flowed into inventory and payables.','The same automation pattern that worked for dispatch could work for receiving.'],cons:['Printed and scanned bills','PACT has no public API','Mismatches must stop before inventory'],bef:[['Bill read by a person','Every line interpreted by eye.'],['Keyed into PACT','Typed as a stock-inward entry.'],['Stock lagged goods','Goods sat before figures caught up.'],['Errors flowed downstream','Into inventory and payables.']],flow:[['Upload','Drop the bill (PDF, photo or scan) onto a web page and pick the sales order. The original is kept in S3.'],['Read','Items, quantities, rates and taxes are extracted and shown for a quick check.'],['Match','Lines are matched to the sales order and the PACT item master; mismatches are flagged before posting.'],['Post inward','The PACT worker creates the stock-inward entry. Stock is correct the moment goods arrive.',1]],note:'Supabase logs every step, so finance can see where a bill is in the flow and why anything was held back.',dec:[['Reuse the dispatch PACT worker','The same proven machine and pattern post stock-inward entries, with the same guards against duplicate posting.','One worker serves both directions; its pace and screens shape both flows.'],['Show extracted lines before posting','Items, quantities, rates and taxes are displayed for a quick check, and mismatches are flagged before anything reaches inventory.','A short human review step remains in the flow, by design.'],['Keep the original bill in S3, linked to the entry','Every PACT entry is one click from the bill that created it, which matters for audits and disputes.','A second store alongside Supabase, in exchange for a complete paper trail.']],ops:[[1,'Mismatches stop before posting','Lines that don\u2019t match the sales order or item master are flagged and held.'],[1,'Status is visible per bill','Supabase records each step, so finance can see where a bill is and why it was held.'],[1,'Duplicate posting guarded','Same guards as the dispatch worker.'],[1,'Complete paper trail','Original in S3, history in Supabase, entry in PACT.']],res:[['Stock right on arrival','Inward entries post as the bill is uploaded, so quantities are accurate the same hour goods arrive.'],['No re-keying','Bill lines go from paper to PACT without typing, and mismatches are caught before inventory.'],['Complete paper trail','Every PACT entry links back to the original bill in S3 and its history in Supabase.']],tools:[['Node.js web app','The upload page and the API that receives bills and tracks status.','A fast, simple front-end that works from any laptop in the store or office.'],['Python','Reads the bill and extracts line items, quantities and taxes.','Strong PDF and image extraction; the same code handles printed and scanned bills.'],['Amazon S3','Stores every original bill.','The bill is one click from the PACT entry it created, which matters for audits and disputes.'],['AWS EC2','Reuses the dispatch PACT worker to post stock-inward entries.','Same proven pattern and machine, with the same guards against duplicate posting.'],['Supabase','Stores bills, extracted lines, match results and status.','Finance can see exactly where every bill is and why anything was held.'],['Vercel','Hosts the upload page.','Always available, nothing to install, instant deploys.'],['PACT ERP','Where the stock-inward entry and inventory live.','Inventory stays in the one system everyone trusts; the tool only removes the keying.']]},
vehicle:{k:'Case 06 / 06 — GPS telemetry',lead:'Follows each delivery vehicle from the factory gate to every stop: how long it took to arrive, how long it stayed, how fast it drove, and a complete summary of the vehicle\u2019s day.',role:'Design, telemetry pipeline, web dashboard',stack:'GPS telemetry · Node.js · Maps · Supabase · Vercel',prob:['The client dispatched vehicles every morning and knew nothing reliable about them until the driver returned. Late deliveries couldn\u2019t be explained, long stops went unnoticed, and there was no record of speed.','They wanted an honest, automatic account of each vehicle\u2019s day without relying on driver reports.'],cons:['No driver input','Points every few seconds','Must explain a late delivery'],bef:[['Vehicles leave','Dispatched every morning.'],['Nothing until return','No reliable information during the day.'],['Unexplained delays','Late deliveries and long stops went unnoticed.'],['No speed record','Nothing factual to coach from.']],flow:[['Track','GPS position and speed arrive every few seconds and are stored with a timestamp.'],['Detect stops','Geofences around the factory, vendors and outlets turn raw points into arrivals and departures.',1],['Measure','Travel time between stops, dwell time at each, speed along the route and over-speed events.'],['Report','A live map during the day and a per-vehicle daily summary at the end of it.']],note:'Daily summary per vehicle: stops visited, time to reach and time at each, driving hours, idle hours, distance, over-speed events.',dec:[['Geofences turn points into events','Arrivals, departures and dwell times come from geofences around the factory, vendors and outlets, not from drivers pressing anything.','Each location needs a fence; a new vendor or outlet means a new geofence.'],['One Node.js codebase for ingestion and dashboard','Receives the stream of small events, applies geofences, computes trip and dwell times, and serves the API.','Ingestion and presentation scale together rather than separately.'],['Postgres for the time-series','Supabase stores telemetry, stops and daily summaries, and keeps history for disputes and planning.','A general-purpose database rather than a dedicated time-series store; fine at this scale.']],ops:[[1,'Over-speed events are logged','Per trip and driver, a factual basis for coaching.'],[1,'History stays available','Telemetry, stops and summaries are kept for disputes and planning.'],[0,'GPS gaps and jitter','A unit that loses signal or jitters near a fence boundary can produce false arrivals; fence sizing and gap handling are reviewed per deployment.']],res:[['Every delivery explained','Arrival, departure and dwell time at each stop are recorded, so late deliveries have a cause.'],['Safer driving','Over-speed events are logged per trip and driver, a factual basis for coaching.'],['A daily record per vehicle','Distance, stops, driving and idle hours, every day, without a form filled in.']],tools:[['GPS telemetry','Position and speed from each vehicle.','An objective record that doesn\u2019t depend on the driver remembering or reporting.'],['Node.js','Receives telemetry, applies geofences, computes trip and dwell times.','Handles a steady stream of small events and serves the dashboard API from one codebase.'],['Maps','Live map and route playback.','Seeing the route makes a late delivery explainable at a glance.'],['Supabase','Stores telemetry, stops and daily summaries.','Postgres handles time-series well, and history stays available for disputes and planning.'],['Vercel','Hosts the dashboard.','The team opens a link on any device; no install, no servers to manage.']]}};
